{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788374330,"nonce":"dxlOq0QToqwOIDWGid/mLDAtv7I=","title":"landmark: rwa README's documented --set.\u003cname\u003e form is refused by the verb","message":"`rwa/README.md` §Argument syntax lists, as a worked example of dotted keys:\n\n    rwa landmark --set.kitchen 120,130\n\nThat expands to `{\"set\":{\"kitchen\":\"120,130\"}}`, and the mod refuses it:\n\n    bad-args / refused: missing required arg 'name' (string)\n\nThe shape the verb actually takes is one landmark per call, with `name` and\n`at` INSIDE `set`:\n\n    {\"set\":{\"name\":\"base-center\",\"at\":\"100,107\"}}\n\nTwo further shapes were probed and both refuse with their own message, so the\nverb is internally consistent — it is only the README that is wrong:\n\n    {\"set\":[{\"name\":..,\"at\":..}]}   -\u003e 'set must be {name, at}'\n    {\"set\":{\"name\":..,\"pos\":..}}    -\u003e \"set needs 'at'\"\n\nCost when it bit (run openrun-20260902, colony start): the natural first\nattempt was a whole-map `{\"set\":{name1:pos1, name2:pos2, ...}}` batch, which\nrefused; the fallback `{\"name\":..,\"at\":..}` **returned ok:true with\n`landmarks: {}`** and journalled an unknown-arg warning naming 'at' and 'name'\nas dropped. So the second attempt looked like a success and registered\nnothing — six landmarks silently absent, found only by reading the journal\nwarning. SESSION-START position 7 is 'landmark — the names plans are written\nin', so a silent no-op here is a whole session written against names that do\nnot resolve.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `rwa/README.md`'s landmark example is the shape the verb accepts, verified\n  by running it against a live bench.\n- Either the verb accepts the dotted `--set.\u003cname\u003e \u003cpos\u003e` form as documented,\n  or the README stops showing it; the two agree, whichever way it is closed.\n- A `landmark` call whose only recognised args were dropped does not return\n  `ok:true` with an empty result — an all-args-dropped call on a MUTATING verb\n  is a refusal, not a success. (This half is the general one and may be split\n  out: the unknown-arg warning already exists and is correct; what is missing\n  is that it does not change the verdict.)","files":null}]}